<!-- Advanced Dashboard Card Layout — “Profile / Project Cards”
1. Dashboard container

Full width (w-full)

Max width large enough for desktops (max-w-7xl)

Centered horizontally (mx-auto)

Padding around the section (p-6)

Optional: a light background for the dashboard (bg-gray-50)

2. Grid layout

Turn the container into a grid

Add gaps between items (gap-6)

Responsive columns:

Mobile → 1 column

Tablet → 2 columns

Desktop → 3 columns

Extra large → 4 columns (optional)

3. Card container

Each card should:

Have rounded corners (rounded-xl)

Have shadow (shadow-lg)

Overflow hidden (for rounded image corners)

Add padding (p-4 or p-5)

Have hover effect to scale (hover:scale-105 + transition-transform)

Background white (bg-white)

4. Card layout (flex inside grid item)

Divide the card horizontally on medium+ screens: image on left, content on right

Use md:flex to make this responsive

On mobile, stack image on top, content below

5. Card image

Image occupies:

Full width on mobile (w-full)

Fixed width on desktop (md:w-48)

Height: fixed (h-48 on mobile, md:h-full on desktop)

Cropped nicely (object-cover)

6. Card content

Vertical padding (p-4 or p-5)

Title: bold, prominent (font-bold text-lg)

Subtitle: smaller, muted (text-gray-500)

Description: paragraph with spacing (mt-2 text-gray-700)

Footer button aligned below content:

Rounded (rounded-full)

Background color (bg-indigo-500)

Hover effect (hover:bg-indigo-600)

Padding (px-4 py-2)

7. Optional additions for complexity

Add status badge (like “Active” / “Completed”) on top-right corner of the card

Use absolute + top-2 right-2 inside a relative card

Badge styling: rounded, colored background, small text

8. Responsive behavior

Grid adjusts columns according to screen width

Cards scale independently on hover without affecting neighbors

Images and content stack nicely on mobile

Buttons remain visible and clickable -->